cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the preprint below (preferred-citation); cite the repository for the code and benchmark data."
title: "ABIOS: Token-Aware Shared-State Messaging for Agent-to-Agent Communication"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Arifuddin
    given-names: Ahraz
    affiliation: Moissanite Labs
  - name: grk-qalam
    affiliation: Moissanite Labs
    note: agent contributor
repository-code: "https://github.com/Moissanite-Labs/abios"
url: "https://github.com/Moissanite-Labs/abios"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  ABIOS is a tokenizer-aware wire encoding family for multi-message agent command
  streams, with decode-sufficient setup accounting, content-addressed refs, and
  reproducible o200k_base benchmarks against JSON, English, TOON, and Agora-style
  baselines. Reference implementation and SPEC-ABIOS-3 ship in the abios repository;
  Synbios forge schema is an example profile only.
keywords:
  - agent-to-agent
  - token optimization
  - messaging protocol
  - abios
  - sym-2p
  - reproducible research
